use std
use ttf
use amni-drive
into cockpit_render.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's Helium + Gold software cockpit and 3D Rolling Dash Dial renderer with real anti-aliased TrueType font rendering via `ttf` (Atkinson Hyperlegible Bold), exact SDF concave-arc crescent wings, and cylindrical 3D perspective barrel shading.
Struct `Canvas` holds `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `px` as a growable byte buffer of length `w * h * 4`.
Module state caches a loaded `ttf::Info` (`FONT_INFO`) and a boolean `FONT_READY` (default false) so the TrueType font is initialized once and reused across every frame and label.
Function `load_font_bytes` takes `data` as a read-only byte slice and returns a boolean. Copy `data` into `FONT_INFO.d`, set `FONT_INFO.fo` to `ttf::font_offset(FONT_INFO.d, 0)` (return false if negative), call `ttf::init(FONT_INFO)`, store result in `FONT_READY`, and return `FONT_READY`.
Function `load_font_file` takes `path` as a read-only byte slice and returns a boolean; reads the file bytes via `std` file read and passes them to `load_font_bytes`.
Function `new_canvas` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `bg` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, returning a `Canvas` filled with `bg`.
Function `shade_color` takes `col` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color and `factor` as a 32-bit float (clamped to `[0.0, 1.4]`), scaling R, G, B by `factor` (clamped to `0..255`) while preserving alpha.
Function `blend_px` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x` and `y` as 32-bit integers, `col` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, and `cov` as a 32-bit float coverage in 0 through 1. Alpha-blend R, G, B over the destination pixel, keeping alpha 255.
Function `sdf_round_rect` takes `px`, `py`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `radius` as 32-bit floats and returns the signed distance to the rounded rectangle.
Function `fill_round_rect` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `radius` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, drawing an anti-aliased rounded rectangle with border stroke.
Function `fill_crescent_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `r` as `layout::Rect`, `radius` as a 32-bit float, `cutout` as `layout::Circle`, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float. Subtract `cutout` via `max(sdf_round_rect, cutout.r - hypot(px - cutout.cx, py - cutout.cy))` when `cutout.r` is greater than 0, and draw anti-aliased fill + continuous border along both straight and concave curved edges.
Function `fill_circle_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, and `ticks` as a boolean. Draw anti-aliased filled circle + border ring; when `ticks` is true draw 36 radial compass ticks around the inner rim (`r - 10` to `r - 3`, longer every 90 degrees).
Function `fill_hex_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `cut` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, drawing an anti-aliased 8-vertex chamfered octagon with border stroke.
Function `draw_sun_icon` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats and `col` as an unsigned 32-bit color; draws a filled sun core (`r * 0.45`) with 8 radial rays.
Function `measure_ttf` takes `text` as a read-only byte slice and `px_h` as a 32-bit float, returning total pixel width as a 32-bit float using `ttf::scale_for(FONT_INFO, px_h)` and summing `f32(ttf::hmetrics(FONT_INFO, g).x) * scale` for each byte in `text`.
Function `draw_text_ttf` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `text` as a read-only byte slice, `x` and `y` as 32-bit floats (`y` is the vertical center of the text line), `px_h` as a 32-bit float, `col` as an unsigned 32-bit color, and `center_x` as a boolean.
If `FONT_READY` is true: compute `scale = ttf::scale_for(FONT_INFO, px_h)`, vertical metrics `vm = ttf::vmetrics(FONT_INFO)` (`ascent = f32(vm.x) * scale`, `descent = f32(vm.y) * scale`), baseline `base_y = y + (ascent + descent) * 0.5` (wait: `descent` is negative in TTF, so `base_y = y + (ascent - (-descent)) * 0.5` — specifically `y + (ascent + descent) * 0.5` centers cap height cleanly!). If `center_x` is true, subtract `measure_ttf(text, px_h) * 0.5` from `pen_x`. For each byte `ch` in `text`: look up `g = ttf::glyph_index(FONT_INFO, int(ch))`, `hm = ttf::hmetrics(FONT_INFO, g)`, `b = ttf::bbox(FONT_INFO, g, scale, scale, 0.0, 0.0)`, `gw = b.x1 - b.x0`, `gh = b.y1 - b.y0`. If `gw > 0` and `gh > 0`, allocate a zeroed byte buffer of size `gw * gh`, call `ttf::glyph_bitmap(FONT_INFO, gbuf, 0, gw, gh, gw, scale, scale, g)`, and composite every nonzero alpha byte onto `c` at `(int(pen_x) + b.x0 + gx, int(base_y) + b.y0 + gy)` via `blend_px` with coverage `f32(alpha) / 255.0`. Advance `pen_x` by `f32(hm.x) * scale`.
If `FONT_READY` is false: fall back cleanly to drawing simple crisp horizontal bar placeholders or 5x7 ASCII bitmaps so text still renders even without a TTF file.
Function `draw_map_graphic` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, `span_w`, and `span_h` as 32-bit floats, `pal` as `look::Palette`, `shade` as a 32-bit float, and `title_px` as a 32-bit float. Draws subtle perspective road lanes in `shade_color(pal.panel2, shade)`, a crisp illuminated navigation chevron in `shade_color(pal.acc, shade)` centered at `(cx, cy)`, `"AMNI-MAP 3D"` above in `shade_color(pal.ink, shade)`, and `"HEADING UP · 0.4 MI"` below in `shade_color(pal.soft, shade)`.
Function `draw_media_content` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `sr` as `layout::Rect`, `pal` as `look::Palette`, `shade` as a 32-bit float, and `ts` as `look::TypeScale`. Centers strictly inside `sr` (`cx = sr.x + sr.w * 0.5`) with balanced vertical rhythm:
- Top 34 percent of `sr`: circular vinyl/album puck (`r = clamp(min(sr.w * 0.22, sr.h * 0.16), 24.0, 56.0)`) with inner ring in `shade_color(pal.acc, shade)`.
- Middle band: `"SPOTIFY"` in `shade_color(pal.acc, shade)` (`meta_px`), `"NIGHT DRIVE"` in `shade_color(pal.ink, shade)` (`title_px`), and a sleek horizontal scrubber bar (`w = min(sr.w * 0.78, 280.0)`, height 6, 58 percent filled in `shade_color(pal.acc, shade)`).
- Bottom band: transport capsule strictly sized to `min(sr.w - 12.0, 260.0)` wide by `clamp(sr.h * 0.17, 44.0, 58.0)` tall, with `<<`, bold `PLAY` pill in `shade_color(pal.acc, shade)`, and `>>` — guaranteed never to exceed `sr`!
Function `draw_drum_3d` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `stage` as `layout::Rect`, `pal` as `look::Palette`, `ts` as `look::TypeScale`, `roll_deg` as a 32-bit float, `speed_mph` as a 32-bit integer, and `temp_f` as a 32-bit integer.
Renders the futuristic 3D Cylindrical Rolling Dash Dial recessed into `stage`:
1. Draw the dark recessed dashboard housing (`stage` rounded rect, radius 26, fill `shade_color(pal.bg, 0.7)`, stroke `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.0`).
2. Draw two brushed metallic roller collars on the left and right edges of `stage` (width 18px, height `stage.h * 0.84` vertically centered) with horizontal knurled grip ticks shifted smoothly by `sin(roll_deg)` so the side rollers visibly spin with the drum!
3. Project all 4 app faces (`app_idx` 0..3) using `drum3d::drum_project_face(i, roll_deg, stage.x + 24.0, stage.y + 10.0, stage.w - 48.0, stage.h - 20.0)`. Sort the visible faces back-to-front by descending `z_depth` (so the front-most active app paints on top!).
4. For each visible `DrumFace`:
   - Compute shaded panel fill `shade_color(pal.panel, f.shade)` and border `shade_color(pal.acc, f.shade)` if `abs(f.rel_deg) < 22.0` else `shade_color(pal.line2, f.shade)`.
   - Draw the perspective-foreshortened curved card centered at `(stage.x + stage.w * 0.5, f.y_center)` with width `f.vis_w`, height `f.vis_h`, and corner radius `clamp(f.vis_h * 0.10, 12.0, 26.0)`.
   - When `f.vis_h >= 64.0`, render the app's live scaled content inside that card (`sr` inset by 14px):
     - `app_idx` 0: `draw_map_graphic` (`"AMNI-MAP 3D"`)
     - `app_idx` 1: `draw_media_content` (`"SPOTIFY · NIGHT DRIVE"`)
     - `app_idx` 2: `"VOICE & APPS"` title + 4 colorful circular app medallions (`MAPS`, `MUSIC`, `PHONE`, `VOICE`) evenly spaced horizontally
     - `app_idx` 3: `"VEHICLE TELEMETRY"` + bold formatted `speed_mph` + `" MPH"` and `temp_f` + `" F"` gauges
   - When `f.vis_h < 64.0` (deeply rolled into the dash slot!), draw just the dimmed app title centered cleanly so it looks sleek and readable as it rolls away!
5. Paint realistic top and bottom **recessed dash-slot shadow vignettes** (36px tall alpha gradient fading from `pal.bg` at top/bottom edge of `stage` to transparent inward) so the 3D barrel looks physically tucked inside the dashboard aperture!
6. Draw 4 crisp vertical detent dots along the right inner bezel showing which app slot is centered (`pal.acc` for active, `pal.dim` for others).
Function `draw_cockpit_at` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers, `preset_key` as a read-only byte slice, `layout_id` and `dock_mode` as 32-bit integers, `speed_mph` and `temp_f` as 32-bit integers, `active_btn` as a 32-bit integer, and `drum_roll_deg` as a 32-bit float, returning a `Canvas`.
Use `look::build_palette(preset_key, 0, false)`, `look::car_type_scale(f32(w), f32(h), 1.0)`, and `layout::compute_cockpit(f32(w), f32(h), ts.min_hit_px, ts.gutter_px, ts.pad_px, layout_id, dock_mode, false)`.
1. Fill canvas with `pal.bg`, draw `plan.dock_rect`, and draw the 6 driver buttons (`"NAV"`, `"MEDIA"`, `"APPS"`, `"VOICE"`, `"3D"`, `"SET"`) using `draw_text_ttf` at `ts.button_px * 0.85` (bold, crisp, zero pixelation!).
2. Pass 1 (primary pods): draw circles (`kind` 0 or 1), hexes, capsules, concave crescent wings, rects, and `kind` 6 (`draw_drum_3d`). Render `draw_map_graphic` inside map pods (`kind` 0) and `draw_media_content` strictly inside `pod.safe_rect` for media pods (`kind` 1).
3. Pass 2 (compact secondary spandrel badges `kind` 2, 3, 4, 5): draw crisp frosted-surface capsules (`fill = pal.panel2`, `stroke = pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 1.4`) with `draw_text_ttf` (`speed_mph` + `" MPH"`, `draw_sun_icon` + `temp_f` + `"F"`, `"11:45 PM"`).
Function `draw_cockpit` calls `draw_cockpit_at` with `drum_roll_deg = 0.0` (keeps full compatibility with existing callers!).
Function `write_ppm` writes binary P6 PPM to `path`.
Function `main` loads `"/home/anmire/ai/amni-drive/helium/fonts/AtkinsonHyperlegible-Bold.ttf"` via `load_font_file`, and renders six preview images into `/tmp/amni_he_preview/`:
1. `honda_800x480_twin_chrono.ppm` (800 by 480, `"amni_dark"`, layout 0, dock 0, speed 65, temp 72, active 1, roll 0.0)
2. `car_1280x720_solar_orbit.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_dark"`, layout 1, dock 0, speed 68, temp 72, active 1, roll 0.0)
3. `car_1280x720_hex_light.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_light"`, layout 4, dock 0, speed 45, temp 74, active 2, roll 0.0)
4. `portrait_720x1280_capsule.ppm` (720 by 1280, `"high_contrast"`, layout 1, dock 1, speed 55, temp 68, active 1, roll 0.0)
5. `car_1280x720_drum3d_rest.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_dark"`, layout 10, dock 0, speed 68, temp 72, active 5, roll 0.0)
6. `car_1280x720_drum3d_swipe.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_dark"`, layout 10, dock 0, speed 68, temp 72, active 5, roll 21.0)
Print `"rendered 6 ttf+3d helium previews ok"` when done.
